{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cdc6d7a7c7e3ddef73b4e0c3c81308973f8ad3b506f59a6a565989e2fdbcaae5","digest":{"component_or_area":"merge recovery toolkit","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/merge_recovery.py","src/rebar/_store/sync.py","src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py","_quarantine_untracked","_restore_local_changes","_merge_abort_named_paths","_untracked_overwrite_paths","_local_change_paths","_quarantine_dir_under","shutil.move","quarantine-move-ok"],"problem_keywords":["code duplication","merge recovery","merge abort","untracked files","quarantine mover","divergence drift"],"propositions":["Merge-abort recovery logic is duplicated across sync.py and push_recovery.py, with the mover re-implemented in both modules causing divergence and repeated bugs","sync.py's _quarantine_untracked lacks the tracked-path verification that push_recovery._quarantine_untracked_paths has, creating a latent defect that appears in multiple callers","push_recovery.py imports pure utility functions from sync.py while re-implementing the mover to use late-bound core._git instead of module-level _git, creating a dependency that blocks refactoring","A unified merge_recovery.py module accepting git as a callable parameter will consolidate the mover and parser, allowing both sync and push_recovery to call one implementation without losing their respective patch points"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787541666056118001,"uuid":"3ac8ae33-93a8-4179-9b83-be3ef18a5b01"}